BT /F3 7.5 Tf 50 660 Td (* Academic Notice: Department guidelines describe a 5-member template; registered team strictly consists of 3 members.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 50 642 Td (Abstract-) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 95 642 Td (The memory wall between processor cycle frequencies and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 631 Td (DRAM latency represents a fundamental computing bottleneck. Cache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 620 Td (memory mitigates this discrepancy by exploiting spatial and temporal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 609 Td (locality. This paper presents the register-transfer level \(RTL\) design) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 598 Td (and functional verification of a 16-bit direct-mapped cache controller) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 587 Td (in Verilog-2001. The architecture interfaces an 8-bit CPU core to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 576 Td (main memory via a 4-line, 4-byte/line \(16 bytes capacity\) SRAM array.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 565 Td (A 6-state FSM coordinates hit detection, allocation, and Write-Through) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 554 Td (with Write-Allocate memory updates. Verification across 20 test) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 543 Td (assertions confirmed 100% pass rate with zero cycle stalls.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 50 528 Td (Keywords- Direct-Mapped Cache, Verilog HDL, FSM, Write-Through.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 510 Td (I. INTRODUCTION) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 497 Td (Modern microprocessors execute multiple instructions per cycle, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 486 Td (DRAM access latencies require dozens of wait cycles [1]. Cache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 475 Td (memories resolve this limitation by storing active memory working) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 464 Td (sets. Direct-mapped caches provide the lowest access latency and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 453 Td (smallest silicon footprint, eliminating complex multi-way multiplexing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 442 Td (and LRU replacement tracking logic [2]. This project implements a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 431 Td (modular, synthesizable 16-bit cache system using Verilog-2001.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 412 Td (II. LITERATURE REVIEW) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 399 Td (Foundational principles of cache memories were established by Smith) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 388 Td ([2], who analyzed line size and miss distributions. Hill and Smith [3]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 377 Td (evaluated associativity trade-offs, proving direct-mapped caches) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 366 Td (achieve superior cycle times due to fast tag checks. Przybylski [4]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 355 Td (formulated analytical hierarchy models, and Jouppi [5] analyzed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 344 Td (conflict miss mitigations. The IEEE 1364-2001 standard [6] governs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 333 Td (the synthesizable RTL constructs utilized in this implementation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 314 Td (III. BACKGROUND & WORKING PRINCIPLES) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 50 301 Td (A. 16-Bit Memory Address Decomposition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 289 Td (The 16-bit CPU physical memory address A[15:0] is partitioned as:) Tj ET
BT /F4 8 Tf 55 276 Td (A[15:0] = Tag[15:4] \(12b\) + Index[3:2] \(2b\) + Offset[1:0] \(2b\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 263 Td (1\) Offset [1:0]: Selects 1 of 4 bytes inside the cache line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 252 Td (2\) Index [3:2]: Directly addresses 1 of the 4 cache lines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 241 Td (3\) Tag [15:4]: Stored in tag SRAM and checked for hit validation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 50 222 Td (B. Write Policy Comparison) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 210 Td (Under Write-Through, CPU writes update both cache and main memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 199 Td (simultaneously. Memory remains coherent at all times, eliminating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 188 Td (dirty bits and eviction write-backs. Under Write-Allocate, write) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 177 Td (misses fetch the target block before applying the write byte.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 315 642 Td (IV. HARDWARE SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 629 Td (The architecture is decomposed into four modular RTL entities:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 616 Td (1\) cache_memory.v: 4 lines x 4 bytes SRAM array, 12b tag array,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 605 Td (   and 1 valid bit per line. Asynchronous read, synchronous write.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 594 Td (2\) cache_controller.v: Master 6-state FSM coordinating handshakes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 583 Td (   decoding address fields, evaluating hits, and managing memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 572 Td (3\) direct_mapped_cache.v: Top-level structural interconnect.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 561 Td (4\) main_memory.v: Behavioral secondary storage with 2-cycle latency.) Tj ET
0.95 g 0.8 G 315 460 245 90 re B
BT /F2 8 Tf 320 538 Td (TABLE I: HARDWARE SPECIFICATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 320 524 Td (Organization: Direct-Mapped \(1-way\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 320 513 Td (Address Width: 16 bits | Data Width: 8 bits) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 320 502 Td (Lines: 4 | Block Size: 4 Bytes | Capacity: 16 Bytes) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 320 491 Td (Tag: 12 bits | Index: 2 bits | Offset: 2 bits) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 320 480 Td (Write Policy: Write-Through | Allocation: Write-Allocate) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 320 469 Td (Language: Verilog-2001 \(IEEE Std 1364-2001\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 315 442 Td (V. FINITE STATE MACHINE DESIGN) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 429 Td (The cache controller executes across six deterministic states:) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 417 Td (1\) S_IDLE \(3'b000\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 395 417 Td (Latches cpu_addr, cpu_rw, cpu_wdata.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 405 Td (2\) S_LOOKUP \(3'b001\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 410 405 Td (Evaluates stored_valid && \(stored_tag==req_tag\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 394 Td (   Read hit transitions to S_COMPLETE. Write hit updates byte) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 383 Td (   and advances to S_WRITE_THROUGH. Miss triggers S_READ_MISS.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 371 Td (3\) S_READ_MISS \(3'b010\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 422 371 Td (Issues 4-byte block read to main memory.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 359 Td (4\) S_ALLOCATE \(3'b011\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 420 359 Td (Writes block & tag to cache. If write,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 348 Td (   updates write byte and proceeds to S_WRITE_THROUGH.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 336 Td (5\) S_WRITE_THROUGH \(3'b100\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 440 336 Td (Commits write to memory.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 324 Td (6\) S_COMPLETE \(3'b101\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 420 324 Td (Pulses cpu_ready=1 and returns to IDLE.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 315 305 Td (VI. INDIVIDUAL TEAM CONTRIBUTIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 292 Td (The project was executed by three registered members:) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 279 Td (- Member 1 [Student 1]:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 415 279 Td (Lead RTL architecture, design of cache_memory,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 268 Td (  cache_controller, top-level integration, and 32-bit archive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 256 Td (- Member 2 [Student 2]:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 415 256 Td (Verification lead, comprehensive testbench \(tb\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 245 Td (  cycle-accurate verification engine, and VCD generation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 315 233 Td (- Member 3 [Student 3]:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 415 233 Td (Main memory model, IEEE paper authoring,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 222 Td (  block diagrams, video deck, and 30-Q viva preparation guide.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 315 203 Td (VII. EXPERIMENTAL VERIFICATION) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 190 Td (All 20 test assertions achieved 100% pass status under cycle-) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 179 Td (accurate evaluation. Detailed results are detailed on Page 2.) Tj ET

