BT /F2 9 Tf 50 460 Td (A. Numerical Analysis of Conflict Misses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 447 Td (Addresses 0x0034 and 0x0044 demonstrate direct-mapped aliasing:) Tj ET
BT /F4 7.5 Tf 50 436 Td (- 0x0034: Tag=12'h003, Index=2'b01 \(Line 1\), Offset=2'b00) Tj ET
BT /F4 7.5 Tf 50 425 Td (- 0x0044: Tag=12'h004, Index=2'b01 \(Line 1\), Offset=2'b00) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 412 Td (Because index bits are identical \(2'b01\), both map to Line 1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 401 Td (Accessing 0x0044 produces a tag mismatch against stored tag 0x003,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 390 Td (evicting block 0x0034-0x0037. Re-accessing 0x0034 in Test 11 confirms) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 379 Td (it is no longer resident, successfully verifying line replacement.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 50 360 Td (B. Latency Metrics) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 347 Td (- Read Hit Latency: 2 clock cycles \(S_IDLE -> S_LOOKUP -> COMPLETE\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 336 Td (- Read Miss Latency: 5 clock cycles \(Includes 2 memory stall cycles\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 325 Td (- Write Hit Latency: 4 clock cycles \(Cache update + memory write\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 314 Td (- Write Miss Latency: 7 clock cycles \(Fetch block + update + write\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 315 460 Td (VIII. LIMITATIONS & PHASE II ROADMAP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 315 447 Td (1\) Conflict Miss Thrashing: Addresses with identical indices cause) Tj ET
